## 3-Minute Zero-Terminal Setup (macOS)

1. **Install `SoundClud.app`**
   - Download **`SoundClud-{{RELEASE_TAG}}-macOS-Universal.dmg`**, open it, and drag **`SoundClud.app`** to **`Applications`**.
   - Launch **`SoundClud`** from **Applications** *(if macOS Gatekeeper prompts on first launch, right-click `SoundClud.app` -> **Open**)*.
2. **Start the Hi-Fi Receiver (1 Click)**
   - Choose **Direct HEOS Network Mode** *(for streaming over Wi-Fi/Ethernet from your Mac to a Denon or Marantz HEOS amplifier)* or **Optical TOSLINK + HEOS Server Mode** *(for a Mac Mini plugged into Optical S/PDIF)*.
   - Click **`Install & Start Receiver`**. Your detected Hi-Fi outputs appear automatically, and the lightweight receiver auto-starts quietly at login.
3. **Add the Browser Extension**
   - Inside **`SoundClud.app`** under **Step 2**, click **`Copy "chrome://extensions" & Open Browser`**, paste **`chrome://extensions`** into your browser address bar, and turn **Developer mode** **ON** (top-right).
   - Click **`Show Extension Folder in Finder`** and drag **`SoundClud Chrome Extension`** onto the `chrome://extensions` tab.
   - Open **[soundcloud.com](https://soundcloud.com)**, click the **SoundClud** cast pill in the bottom player bar (or toolbar icon), and pick your **HEOS Amplifier** or **Optical Out**.

